※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ A function of the system's convention handed over as a value: a call through a
※ value follows the language's own, so something stands between the two -- the
※ one function that still has a shim.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[cdecl]
fn tripled(x: u64) → u64:
    x × 3u64

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let f: fn(u64) → u64 = tripled
    if f(2u64) = 6u64: 0u6 else: 1u6
